{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the excess of the curtain of the tent shall hang over.</b> Over the curtains of the Mishkan — the curtains of the 'tent' are the upper ones of goats' hair, which are called 'tent,' as it says of them 'for a tent over the Mishkan.' And every 'tent' said of them means nothing but a roof, for they roof and cover over the lower ones. And they extended beyond the lower ones by half a curtain's width to the west — for the half of one curtain, the extra ten, was folded back toward the front of the tent; two cubits' width remained, half of it extending beyond the width of the lower ones." "<b>Shall hang over the back of the Mishkan.</b> To cover the two cubits that were exposed on the boards." "<b>The back of the Mishkan.</b> That is the western side, because the entrance is on the east, that being its front; and north and south are called sides, right and left."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:44.670982464Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}